id: taser
name: Taser
kind: gear
tags: tech
craftDC: Qualified
# "You can spend 1 Action while you possess this Item to target a Character within your Melee
# Range. Make a Clash (Strike vs Strike/Dodge). If you win, that Character has their Life Points
# reduced by the Recorded Ingenuity and then you make a Clash (Recorded Ingenuity vs Corporeal)
# against that character. If you win, that Character is knocked Prone until the start of your next
# turn. They cannot remove the Prone Combat Condition inflicted by a Taser until then."
placeCost: 1
clashRoll: strike
# The first Clash won: the Recorded Ingenuity off their Life Points, and a second Clash - the
# Recorded Ingenuity against their Corporeal - for the Condition.
clashDamage: recorded
clashSecond: corporeal
clashReach: melee
clashCondition: prone
clashUntil: start
clashHold: tased
# "You can increase the Craft DC to Expert to increase your Melee Range by 3 when using this
# Basic Item." Chosen on the Item.
upgradeCraftDC: Expert
upgradeReach: 3
# Its Details. Device: it records its creator's Ingenuity (or a Gear Kit's Score Limit).
details: technology, device
source: Core Rule
description: >
  An Action at someone in your Melee Range: win a Clash (Strike vs Strike/Dodge) and they lose the
  Recorded Ingenuity in Life Points; win a second (Recorded Ingenuity vs Corporeal) and they are
  Prone until the start of your next turn, and cannot get up before then.
text: >
  Taser [Tech]: A handheld object that can be used to incapacitate an enemy.
  –Craft DC: Qualified
  –Details: Technology, Device
  –Effects: You can spend 1 Action while you possess this Item to target a Character within
  your Melee Range. Make a Clash (Strike vs Strike/Dodge). If you win, that Character has their
  Life Points reduced by the Recorded Ingenuity and then you make a Clash (Recorded Ingenuity vs
  Corporeal) against that character. If you win, that Character is knocked Prone until the start
  of your next turn. They cannot remove the Prone Combat Condition inflicted by a Taser until
  then.

  You can increase the Craft DC to Expert to increase your Melee Range by 3 when using this
  Basic Item.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Use: 1 Action at the one character targeted, who has to be within the user's Melee Range -
# measured the way a Physical Attack's is, and not enforced where nothing can be measured. The
# Clash is the Strike Clash the Grapple Check and the Thrust use: the target answers with
# their Strike or their Dodge.
#
# Won, the Recorded Ingenuity comes off their Life Points (a Life Point reduction: no Soak, no Damage
# Reduction), and a second card opens: a Clash of the Recorded Ingenuity against their Corporeal
# Saving Throw. Won, they are Prone until the start of the user's next turn, on the user's clock -
# and Tased as well, a mark that holds the Prone in place (`holds: prone` in its file): standing up
# is refused until the mark runs out, which it does just before the Prone does.
#
# The Expert Taser is a choice on the Item: ticked, its Craft DC reads Expert and it reaches 3
# Squares further. How it was made is between the player and the ARC.
